<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Taiwan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Taiwan is a large island off the south-eastern coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> established a colony there in the seventeenth century but lost it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koxinga">Koxinga</a>'s forces in 1662, and the Qing took the island from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zheng-family">Zheng family</a> in 1683. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-sino-japanese-war">First Sino-Japanese War</a> of 1894–1895 it became a Japanese colony, supplying <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a>.</p></div>
